*** Settings ***
Documentation     Acceptance tests on SYNTHETIC logs with known ground truth.
...
...               These logs are generated by scripts/make_synthetic.py and are not real
...               recordings (see data/SOURCES.md). They cover what the real logs cannot:
...               a cold start, a long static session and a day/year rollover.
Library           GnssLibrary.py

*** Test Cases ***
Cold Start Has A 30-Second Time To First Fix
    Given the synthetic log "SYNTHETIC-cold-start.log"
    When the log is analysed
    Then time to first fix is 30 seconds
    And fix availability is 75.0 %
    And 0 fix-lost events reported

Long Static Session Matches Gaussian CEP Theory
    [Documentation]    sigma = 1 m per axis: CEP50 = 1.177 m, CEP95 = 2.448 m.
    ...                With 600 epochs, 10 % is more than 3 sampling standard deviations.
    Given the synthetic log "SYNTHETIC-static-10min.log"
    When the log is analysed against the true position
    Then CEP50 is within 10 % of 1.177 m
    And CEP95 is within 10 % of 2.448 m

Log Crossing Into A New Year Has One Rollover
    Given the synthetic log "SYNTHETIC-midnight-rollover.log"
    When the log is analysed
    Then 1 UTC day rollover reported
    And all 121 epochs are 1 second apart
    And no integrity problems reported

Cold Start With A Later Outage
    Given the synthetic log "SYNTHETIC-cold-start.log"
    And a 20-second outage starting at 60 s
    When the log is analysed
    Then time to first fix is 30 seconds
    And 1 fix-lost event reported
    And the outage lasts 20 seconds
    And fix availability is 58.3 %
